(3745844, 524079, 30982, '<td valign="top">Like a slow procession, they''re moving in, those gray stones.  For now, the grass, lovingly cut in nice straight and even lines, is holding its own, though.</td>', 'Like a slow procession, they''re moving in, those gray stones.  For now, the grass, lovingly cut in nice straight and even lines, is holding its own, though.', '2007-06-06 08:24:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3745848, 523102, 30982, '<td valign="top">Your ones and twos are from either the "no nudes" crowd, or the "no science in my religion crowd".  You done good with this - I''m paricularly impressed with the clarity of the projection onto an uneven surface, and the lighting and exposure is very nice!</td>', 'Your ones and twos are from either the "no nudes" crowd, or the "no science in my religion crowd".  You done good with this - I''m paricularly impressed with the clarity of the projection onto an uneven surface, and the lighting and exposure is very nice!', '2007-06-06 08:26:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3745853, 524142, 30982, '<td valign="top">David - bring this up in the Team Suck thread and explain how you save and resize for web - we''ll help you figure it out!<br/> <br/>Very good choice for the challenge, by the way - almost looks as though the cross is floating above the pages.  A bit more pronounced shadow would have given this even more emphasis.  By the way, check out the average from commenters!</td>', 'David - bring this up in the Team Suck thread and explain how you save and resize for web - we''ll help you figure it out! Very good choice for the challenge, by the way - almost looks as though the cross is floating above the pages.  A bit more pronounced shadow would have given this even more emphasis.  By the way, check out the average from commenters!', '2007-06-06 08:28:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3745858, 522562, 30982, '<td valign="top">DPC''ers generally don''t like statues, but this is an exceptionally well captured one, in my opinion.  You run the risk of the "but it''s just someone else''s art" issue, but I think in this case the angle you chose and the lighting really do give this a sense of life and a sort of power.</td>', 'DPC''ers generally don''t like statues, but this is an exceptionally well captured one, in my opinion.  You run the risk of the "but it''s just someone else''s art" issue, but I think in this case the angle you chose and the lighting really do give this a sense of life and a sort of power.', '2007-06-06 08:30:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3745866, 521445, 69448, '<td valign="top">Terrific picture! I like the texture and the light. Where is this photo taken?</td>', 'Terrific picture! I like the texture and the light. Where is this photo taken?', '2007-06-06 08:32:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3745885, 522762, 62187, '<td valign="top">I feel this comment is the sum of my feelings - <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jprhea25:</b></div><hr/><i> I feel it was a poor choice to use the Wiccan of symbol the five pointed star (which represents the 4 Elements ruled over by Spirit) inverted or otherwise for you''re Anti-Christian symbol. An upside down cross would have been much more appropriate. May I suggest that next time you do your homework and not perpetuate the misinformation of Hollywood and the medieval Catholic church. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Here''s a quote of yours - ''the Pentagram was the easiest one to draw'' - it''s a Pentacle - NOT a Pentagram.<br/> <br/>Ok, here''s a comment about the photo alone disregarding the subject matter. It''s not bad I would have given it a 7 had I voted in this challenge. Blue Moon is right about ''painting with light'' however, my personal feeling is it''s not cool. Adding to jprhea25''s comment - if you would have inverted the Pentacle, then it would have represented the titles implications - Satanism. The Pentacle is not an anti-christian symbol. It is a symbol for Earth-based ''religions''. It is a symbol I wear. Your photo did well in the challenge - another testament that people in general are mostly gazers.<br/> <br/>Once, somebody made a comment to one of my photos that the title was offensive. Just to let you know, I don''t find your photo/title offensive - just misrepresentive. To bad it''s now forever carved in stone in the DPC records. Please, be more careful next time and Brightest Blessings to you.</td>', 'I feel this comment is the sum of my feelings - Originally posted by jprhea25: I feel it was a poor choice to use the Wiccan of symbol the five pointed star (which represents the 4 Elements ruled over by Spirit) inverted or otherwise for you''re Anti-Christian symbol. An upside down cross would have been much more appropriate. May I suggest that next time you do your homework and not perpetuate the misinformation of Hollywood and the medieval Catholic church.   Here''s a quote of yours - ''the Pentagram was the easiest one to draw'' - it''s a Pentacle - NOT a Pentagram. Ok, here''s a comment about the photo alone disregarding the subject matter. It''s not bad I would have given it a 7 had I voted in this challenge. Blue Moon is right about ''painting with light'' however, my personal feeling is it''s not cool. Adding to jprhea25''s comment - if you would have inverted the Pentacle, then it would have represented the titles implications - Satanism. The Pentacle is not an anti-christian symbol. It is a symbol for Earth-based ''religions''. It is a symbol I wear. Your photo did well in the challenge - another testament that people in general are mostly gazers. Once, somebody made a comment to one of my photos that the title was offensive. Just to let you know, I don''t find your photo/title offensive - just misrepresentive. To bad it''s now forever carved in stone in the DPC records. Please, be more careful next time and Brightest Blessings to you.', '2007-06-06 08:45:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3745892, 523519, 57378, '<td valign="top">This should have been Blue...</td>', 'This should have been Blue...', '2007-06-06 08:50:12.000000', NULL, 0),
