(3746404, 523997, 61961, '<td valign="top">I was really struck by the light and mood of this photo (I gave it an 8), but there is something "off" with the composition that I still can''t be sure of.  I think it is how the top of the man''s head meets the top of the wall and aligns with the bottom of the church -- almost as if the church building is sitting on his head.  Move his hands a bit and you''d have a complete optical illusion of him holding the church, Atlas-like.<br/> <br/>Surprising how many people commented on the sweater!</td>', 'I was really struck by the light and mood of this photo (I gave it an 8), but there is something "off" with the composition that I still can''t be sure of.  I think it is how the top of the man''s head meets the top of the wall and aligns with the bottom of the church -- almost as if the church building is sitting on his head.  Move his hands a bit and you''d have a complete optical illusion of him holding the church, Atlas-like. Surprising how many people commented on the sweater!', '2007-06-06 10:55:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3746414, 524017, 61961, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Man_Called_Horse:</b></div><hr/><i> sorry, but as a photographer your job is to convince me.<br/>photographically, this is a nice picture. However, I am not convinced that this is religious. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>He said this to nearly EVERYONE!  LOL<br/> <br/>Anyway, congratulations on placing so highly.  I loved this photo (it was one of my 10s).  No suggestions for improvement.  Well done.</td>', 'Originally posted by Man_Called_Horse: sorry, but as a photographer your job is to convince me.photographically, this is a nice picture. However, I am not convinced that this is religious.  He said this to nearly EVERYONE!  LOL Anyway, congratulations on placing so highly.  I loved this photo (it was one of my 10s).  No suggestions for improvement.  Well done.', '2007-06-06 10:58:26.000000', NULL, 0),
