(3763544, 524065, 55838, '<td valign="top">I see your sense of humor shining through on this shot somehow.  I really like the treatment on the sky.  A little tall and skinny perhaps - it seems like square(ish) crops open bigger and capture the higher votes (I''m sure a square crop would not work for a tower shot like this - just more of a general comment).  So I guess we know how Zeuss feels about religion! : )  Edit - forgot to mention that I did not vote on this image.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-06-10 15:18:36.</i></td>', 'I see your sense of humor shining through on this shot somehow.  I really like the treatment on the sky.  A little tall and skinny perhaps - it seems like square(ish) crops open bigger and capture the higher votes (I''m sure a square crop would not work for a tower shot like this - just more of a general comment).  So I guess we know how Zeuss feels about religion! : )  Edit - forgot to mention that I did not vote on this image.', '2007-06-10 16:18:12.000000', '2007-06-10 16:18:36.000000', 0),
(3764024, 522669, 68035, '<td valign="top">Michelle<br/> <br/>Well I will be honest and say I thought that this image whilst good was not great (please understand I thought it was good though --- I gave it 6)<br/> <br/>However the poigniancy of the story is incredible and knowing what I do now about the image really adds to it<br/> <br/>I guess true faith is recognising that such things occur is down to failings in man rather than God<br/> <br/></td>', 'Michelle Well I will be honest and say I thought that this image whilst good was not great (please understand I thought it was good though --- I gave it 6) However the poigniancy of the story is incredible and knowing what I do now about the image really adds to it I guess true faith is recognising that such things occur is down to failings in man rather than God ', '2007-06-10 19:00:18.000000', NULL, 0),
