(3777490, 519422, 12611, '<td valign="top">Excellent shot; its good to see that there are still those who will go out on a limb for mystery; adventure.</td>', 'Excellent shot; its good to see that there are still those who will go out on a limb for mystery; adventure.', '2007-06-13 08:16:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3777494, 523615, 12611, '<td valign="top">Excellent; underrated in my opinion. Beautiful sky- would make an excellent print.</td>', 'Excellent; underrated in my opinion. Beautiful sky- would make an excellent print.', '2007-06-13 08:18:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3779956, 524202, 62787, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club. <br/> <br/>I gave this image a 5 during voting, and on second look, I think I underrated it. The composition is interesting, and there''s lovely geometry present in the picture.<br/> <br/>Conceptually it works well. The religious belief content of the picture is obvious, but effective - yes, divine light, lit from above, etc. The angle and composition work very well for this. Another thing that could be read into it is that everything in the picture comes in 3''s, so there could be a reference to Jesus and the holy trinity in there somewhere. <br/> <br/>However, what doesn''t work well for me about this picture is that Jesus doesn''t come across effectively as the main subject of the picture. A viewer''s eye tends to go towards the areas of highlight first, so the first thing I looked at were the 3 little round windows, which seem to be a bit too prominent. The eye then travels towards the big glass window/ceiling thing, and you only notice Jesus as a sort of afterthought. Now, since this is in advanced editing, there''s a considerable amount of control you have over this in pp - using a soft light layer and painting white across jesus and black across all the windows (and playing with the opacity to make the adjustments subtle) would have potentially improved the picture a lot. Also, burning the shadows on the statue at a low opacity can make the picture subtly more dramatic.<br/> <br/>Also, a technical point: overall the exposure is good, but some of the window highlights seem a bit blown, using a shorter exposure might have helped. Even if it gives a slightly underexposed picture, you can bring out the subject in pp, whereas blown highlights are difficult to get rid of.<br/> <br/>Overall I''d say this is an interesting entry which scored well, but with some improvements, it could have done even better. Well done anyway.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club.  I gave this image a 5 during voting, and on second look, I think I underrated it. The composition is interesting, and there''s lovely geometry present in the picture. Conceptually it works well. The religious belief content of the picture is obvious, but effective - yes, divine light, lit from above, etc. The angle and composition work very well for this. Another thing that could be read into it is that everything in the picture comes in 3''s, so there could be a reference to Jesus and the holy trinity in there somewhere.  However, what doesn''t work well for me about this picture is that Jesus doesn''t come across effectively as the main subject of the picture. A viewer''s eye tends to go towards the areas of highlight first, so the first thing I looked at were the 3 little round windows, which seem to be a bit too prominent. The eye then travels towards the big glass window/ceiling thing, and you only notice Jesus as a sort of afterthought. Now, since this is in advanced editing, there''s a considerable amount of control you have over this in pp - using a soft light layer and painting white across jesus and black across all the windows (and playing with the opacity to make the adjustments subtle) would have potentially improved the picture a lot. Also, burning the shadows on the statue at a low opacity can make the picture subtly more dramatic. Also, a technical point: overall the exposure is good, but some of the window highlights seem a bit blown, using a shorter exposure might have helped. Even if it gives a slightly underexposed picture, you can bring out the subject in pp, whereas blown highlights are difficult to get rid of. Overall I''d say this is an interesting entry which scored well, but with some improvements, it could have done even better. Well done anyway.', '2007-06-13 19:47:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3779992, 521582, 62787, '<td valign="top">Wow, just noticed this came 35th at a 5.9 score?! The DPL really is doing strange things... Well done though, that picture deserved to do well :)</td>', 'Wow, just noticed this came 35th at a 5.9 score?! The DPL really is doing strange things... Well done though, that picture deserved to do well :)', '2007-06-13 19:55:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3780067, 519549, 62787, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>I gave this image a 4 during voting. But looking at your comments and scores, there seems to be a bunch of people who appreciated it a lot more than I did, so I guess it might be down to personal preference.<br/> <br/>I did like the concept - it fits the challenge perfectly, but in an original way. The old bible is perfect for the shot, and the composition is good - it''s like the bible is asking to be followed. <br/> <br/>My biggest objection was to the lighting. It seems really quite harsh at the bottom right, and it''s coming from an angle which still leaves the fishing rods somewhat indistinct. I also thought the dark bits at the back were too much in contrast with the harsh lighting at the front. I guess I would have preferred either light coming from the top right corner of the picture (cliched divine light metaphor style of thing, probably not that great for lighting up the subject matter), or a similar enough layout, but slightly more subtly, evenly done - where there are still highlights and shadows, but the front is more gently lit, and the back isn''t completely black. I would''ve been tempted to light-paint the subject using a flashlight - that gives you some interesting options.<br/> <br/>I also would have prefered a slightly different camera angle - maybe raising it slightly so that the Bible looks a bit less flat and the figure was brought to life a bit more. <br/> <br/>However, as I said, I do seem to be representing a minority view, so there are probably a lot of people who really liked the features I find objectionable...<br/> <br/>Well done on an interesting entry anyway :)</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. I gave this image a 4 during voting. But looking at your comments and scores, there seems to be a bunch of people who appreciated it a lot more than I did, so I guess it might be down to personal preference. I did like the concept - it fits the challenge perfectly, but in an original way. The old bible is perfect for the shot, and the composition is good - it''s like the bible is asking to be followed.  My biggest objection was to the lighting. It seems really quite harsh at the bottom right, and it''s coming from an angle which still leaves the fishing rods somewhat indistinct. I also thought the dark bits at the back were too much in contrast with the harsh lighting at the front. I guess I would have preferred either light coming from the top right corner of the picture (cliched divine light metaphor style of thing, probably not that great for lighting up the subject matter), or a similar enough layout, but slightly more subtly, evenly done - where there are still highlights and shadows, but the front is more gently lit, and the back isn''t completely black. I would''ve been tempted to light-paint the subject using a flashlight - that gives you some interesting options. I also would have prefered a slightly different camera angle - maybe raising it slightly so that the Bible looks a bit less flat and the figure was brought to life a bit more.  However, as I said, I do seem to be representing a minority view, so there are probably a lot of people who really liked the features I find objectionable... Well done on an interesting entry anyway :)', '2007-06-13 20:11:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3780271, 523102, 76198, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! You''re the first person to take advantage of my newfound Critique Club status. Hopefully it''ll be helpful, and feel free to reply with a critique of my critique!<br/> <br/><b>Pros:</b> <br/> <br/>This is a fairly compelling image; the juxtaposition of images on the human body is a technique that always works in getting an emotional reaction from me, anyway. And I think your choice of image and the layout work well - the centered DNA and the coding. Obviously the voters liked it too, as you scored well above the challenge average of 5.32 and in the 80% percentile.<br/> <br/><b>Cons:</b> <br/> <br/>For me there are three things that stand out: Skin tone, hair tone, and the relationship with the background. Colorwise there''s something not quite ''right'' with the skin and hair; both seem a little washed out; the hair in particular could use some additional lighting. It sounds like you did what you could with it, given the image you ended up with. And the way the body sits against the background looks almost "cut and paste" to me; I don''t think it is, but the edges look off. Unfortunately I lack the expertise to recommend a solution! <br/> <br/><b>The challenge:</b> <br/> <br/>This is a toughy, as you acknowledge in your notes. I''ll approach the image''s relationship to the challenge from three directions: <br/> <br/>"How does it sit with me?" - I can tell you that as a scientist and atheist the conflation of science and religeon is a touchy subject, and had I voted on this one I would have been uncomfortable with the subject and title in this challenge (or in the science one! ;) )<br/> <br/>"How did it sit with voters?" - clearly some controversy, as this has a pretty high voting spread, and several DNMC comments.<br/> <br/>"How did it sit with you?" - this is really what matters, and from your description it sounds like you said what you hoped to say with it - and of this you should be proud! <br/> <br/>Congrats on a great image, and thanks for the opportunity to critique it.</td>', 'Congratulations! You''re the first person to take advantage of my newfound Critique Club status. Hopefully it''ll be helpful, and feel free to reply with a critique of my critique! Pros:  This is a fairly compelling image; the juxtaposition of images on the human body is a technique that always works in getting an emotional reaction from me, anyway. And I think your choice of image and the layout work well - the centered DNA and the coding. Obviously the voters liked it too, as you scored well above the challenge average of 5.32 and in the 80% percentile. Cons:  For me there are three things that stand out: Skin tone, hair tone, and the relationship with the background. Colorwise there''s something not quite ''right'' with the skin and hair; both seem a little washed out; the hair in particular could use some additional lighting. It sounds like you did what you could with it, given the image you ended up with. And the way the body sits against the background looks almost "cut and paste" to me; I don''t think it is, but the edges look off. Unfortunately I lack the expertise to recommend a solution!  The challenge:  This is a toughy, as you acknowledge in your notes. I''ll approach the image''s relationship to the challenge from three directions:  "How does it sit with me?" - I can tell you that as a scientist and atheist the conflation of science and religeon is a touchy subject, and had I voted on this one I would have been uncomfortable with the subject and title in this challenge (or in the science one! ;) ) "How did it sit with voters?" - clearly some controversy, as this has a pretty high voting spread, and several DNMC comments. "How did it sit with you?" - this is really what matters, and from your description it sounds like you said what you hoped to say with it - and of this you should be proud!  Congrats on a great image, and thanks for the opportunity to critique it.', '2007-06-13 21:18:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3780308, 523175, 76198, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club! This is my second image ever to critique, and, well... wow! <br/> <br/><b>Pros:</b> <br/> <br/>Well, if you''re looking for a powerful, viceral image, this works - it does inspire a strong reaction. And the fake (please let it be fake) puke looks very good. <br/> <br/><b>Cons:</b> <br/> <br/>I think you know the answers here, but first of all you (as you knew going in) turned off a lot of voters; DPC voters don''t vote high for "ick" as an emotion. The composition is also very busy; if the "humor and shock" element were removed I don''t think you''d see many people defending the "artistic quality" of the piece; I also don''t think that''s what you were going for as your portfolio makes it abundantly clear that you know how to take an aesthetically pleasing shot. <br/> <br/><b>Challenge:</b> <br/> <br/>I, for one, appreciate creative takes on challenges, and as an atheist am not bothered by your message particularly... but again from the voters perspective you''re going to turn some people off with this take of what is a very serious subject to many. <br/> <br/>Overall, I think you knew what you were signing up for when you submitted!<br/> <br/>-Evan</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club! This is my second image ever to critique, and, well... wow!  Pros:  Well, if you''re looking for a powerful, viceral image, this works - it does inspire a strong reaction. And the fake (please let it be fake) puke looks very good.  Cons:  I think you know the answers here, but first of all you (as you knew going in) turned off a lot of voters; DPC voters don''t vote high for "ick" as an emotion. The composition is also very busy; if the "humor and shock" element were removed I don''t think you''d see many people defending the "artistic quality" of the piece; I also don''t think that''s what you were going for as your portfolio makes it abundantly clear that you know how to take an aesthetically pleasing shot.  Challenge:  I, for one, appreciate creative takes on challenges, and as an atheist am not bothered by your message particularly... but again from the voters perspective you''re going to turn some people off with this take of what is a very serious subject to many.  Overall, I think you knew what you were signing up for when you submitted! -Evan', '2007-06-13 21:31:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(3780537, 519763, 71189, '<td valign="top">why ISO 1600?</td>', 'why ISO 1600?', '2007-06-13 22:52:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3780629, 523915, 24951, '<td valign="top">Thank you</td>', 'Thank you', '2007-06-13 23:21:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3780865, 523175, 61552, '<td valign="top">Yup, you''re right!  I knew it wouldn''t score well, but I couldn''t resist.  Yes, the puke is fake.  Chicken dumpling soup and BBQ sauce for the color.  Thank you!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-06-13 23:51:22.</i></td>', 'Yup, you''re right!  I knew it wouldn''t score well, but I couldn''t resist.  Yes, the puke is fake.  Chicken dumpling soup and BBQ sauce for the color.  Thank you!', '2007-06-14 00:49:42.000000', '2007-06-14 00:51:22.000000', 0),
(3781433, 523701, 68035, '<td valign="top">Alicia<br/> <br/>Woah I somehow missed that this one scored so high (I think I am starting to subconsciously ignore your images :-) )<br/> <br/>Good job here, cracking sky and lovely perspective</td>', 'Alicia Woah I somehow missed that this one scored so high (I think I am starting to subconsciously ignore your images :-) ) Good job here, cracking sky and lovely perspective', '2007-06-14 02:06:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3782088, 523280, 48389, '<td valign="top">What an interesting little fellow! Nice composition and I love the old and new in this shot! :o)</td>', 'What an interesting little fellow! Nice composition and I love the old and new in this shot! :o)', '2007-06-14 05:30:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3782089, 524043, 48389, '<td valign="top">It certainly doesnt look like this was very easy to do at all!! A great expression of an aspect of religion and interesting to read your words underneath! :o)</td>', 'It certainly doesnt look like this was very easy to do at all!! A great expression of an aspect of religion and interesting to read your words underneath! :o)', '2007-06-14 05:31:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3782099, 524065, 48389, '<td valign="top">An interesting building, I love the bells! :o) Clever position of the sign too...sorry this didn''t score better for you but so glad you are part of our team Sonya!:o)</td>', 'An interesting building, I love the bells! :o) Clever position of the sign too...sorry this didn''t score better for you but so glad you are part of our team Sonya!:o)', '2007-06-14 05:38:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3783041, 523425, 63269, '<td valign="top">i love your post-processing here - neat shot!</td>', 'i love your post-processing here - neat shot!', '2007-06-14 11:06:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3786315, 523517, 64994, '<td valign="top">Jon, another great shot! I LOVE the sky in this, it really sets it off! I really think the centered comp, works very well here as well!! Great capture, would have made a great Candid entry as well!!!</td>', 'Jon, another great shot! I LOVE the sky in this, it really sets it off! I really think the centered comp, works very well here as well!! Great capture, would have made a great Candid entry as well!!!', '2007-06-14 23:22:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3786763, 519465, 36006, '<td valign="top">What you know, and what I see are two different things.<br/> <br/>As a photographer, you have to portray what you know in the frame.<br/> <br/>I do not have ESP. I don''t know different religious rituals. <br/> <br/>In this image, all that I see is a man on a stoop, leaning over water.<br/> <br/>For all I know, he is using the water as a mirror. For all I know, this man is getting cool by a fountain. For all I know, he is readying himself to dive in the water.<br/> <br/>There is nothing here that explains what you want to show me.<br/> <br/></td>', 'What you know, and what I see are two different things. As a photographer, you have to portray what you know in the frame. I do not have ESP. I don''t know different religious rituals.  In this image, all that I see is a man on a stoop, leaning over water. For all I know, he is using the water as a mirror. For all I know, this man is getting cool by a fountain. For all I know, he is readying himself to dive in the water. There is nothing here that explains what you want to show me. ', '2007-06-15 01:04:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3790131, 524096, 65858, '<td valign="top">=)  A new comment...  Should show &gt;&gt;3&lt;&lt; in your profile view.</td>', '=)  A new comment...  Should show >>3<< in your profile view.', '2007-06-15 23:08:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3792356, 523350, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot. Your compositon and contrast are great.</td>', 'Very nice shot. Your compositon and contrast are great.', '2007-06-16 22:30:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3793552, 523968, 74078, '<td valign="top">Nice image. You mentioned that you wished that the angle wings could be more visible. Perhaps with a similar composition but with your model standing side on, facing perhaps to the left of the frame would give a better representation of what you were trying to convey to the viewer. Great shot though and nice processing. After finding one of your images earlier today, I am enjoying looking through the remainder of your gallery. Awesome work</td>', 'Nice image. You mentioned that you wished that the angle wings could be more visible. Perhaps with a similar composition but with your model standing side on, facing perhaps to the left of the frame would give a better representation of what you were trying to convey to the viewer. Great shot though and nice processing. After finding one of your images earlier today, I am enjoying looking through the remainder of your gallery. Awesome work', '2007-06-17 11:48:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3794777, 521376, 23484, '<td valign="top">I really like the high contrast. Nice job Mary.</td>', 'I really like the high contrast. Nice job Mary.', '2007-06-17 21:02:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3794781, 520468, 23484, '<td valign="top">I think this is a cool shot and in MY opinion, I think it meets the challenge well. Everybody worships in their own way.</td>', 'I think this is a cool shot and in MY opinion, I think it meets the challenge well. Everybody worships in their own way.', '2007-06-17 21:05:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3794824, 521511, 23484, '<td valign="top">Deb, this is such a beautiful shot.  I absolutely love it. The colors are so beautiful and the sharpness is impecable. Great job and great score.</td>', 'Deb, this is such a beautiful shot.  I absolutely love it. The colors are so beautiful and the sharpness is impecable. Great job and great score.', '2007-06-17 21:11:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3797281, 519818, 57060, '<td valign="top">Wow, didn''t see this one during voting - but I agree with the commenters, this is an exceptional image. Definately not DPC material but clearly that cannot be a criteria for judgement regarding great images like this.<br/> <br/>Jack</td>', 'Wow, didn''t see this one during voting - but I agree with the commenters, this is an exceptional image. Definately not DPC material but clearly that cannot be a criteria for judgement regarding great images like this. Jack', '2007-06-18 10:20:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3797713, 523776, 70888, '<td valign="top">shouldve saved this shot for the negative space challenge,this is <i>great</i> use of it.nicely composed,conceived...</td>', 'shouldve saved this shot for the negative space challenge,this is great use of it.nicely composed,conceived...', '2007-06-18 12:10:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3797889, 522839, 24454, '<td valign="top">Oh man!!!   I can''t believe this only scored 5.1!!!   I love this photo so much.  It''s a perfect moment capturing religion.    I''m really disappointed that this didn''t score better!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Oh man!!!   I can''t believe this only scored 5.1!!!   I love this photo so much.  It''s a perfect moment capturing religion.    I''m really disappointed that this didn''t score better! ', '2007-06-18 12:58:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3798752, 522979, 62187, '<td valign="top">The colors and focus appear good to me. I think you did do your homework on this photo - the inverted Pentacle is (imho) a representation of ''Satanism'' and where some may disagree, the Bible is something good. Brightest Blessings!</td>', 'The colors and focus appear good to me. I think you did do your homework on this photo - the inverted Pentacle is (imho) a representation of ''Satanism'' and where some may disagree, the Bible is something good. Brightest Blessings!', '2007-06-18 17:22:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3805541, 523521, 19708, '<td valign="top">Only belief I have is that this is a beautiful photograph.</td>', 'Only belief I have is that this is a beautiful photograph.', '2007-06-20 03:15:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3818693, 523435, 41337, '<td valign="top">Nice shot! I thought about entering a shot of Saint Mary Cathedral.</td>', 'Nice shot! I thought about entering a shot of Saint Mary Cathedral.', '2007-06-22 01:08:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3825117, 523064, 31637, '<td valign="top">Nice and even. Good exposure and focus.</td>', 'Nice and even. Good exposure and focus.', '2007-06-23 17:59:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3826987, 522413, 48228, '<td valign="top">So rich in color, textures and patterns. This really goes suit the challenge thats for sure..... You did a good job with this one.....</td>', 'So rich in color, textures and patterns. This really goes suit the challenge thats for sure..... You did a good job with this one.....', '2007-06-24 08:28:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3829776, 520644, 69008, '<td valign="top">I like the way you used the trees to cover a lot of the bright sky, and to frame the church. Shooting at a different time of day would give a shot from this same point a completely different look and feel. The backlight works well with your title in this case.<br/>It looks like the lights on each side of the entrance are on?  In archetectual shots like this, in order to get the lights to look good at dusk or after dark, a long exposure is used, and someone flips the lights on and off for just a blink. They show up good, and don''t blow out completely that way.</td>', 'I like the way you used the trees to cover a lot of the bright sky, and to frame the church. Shooting at a different time of day would give a shot from this same point a completely different look and feel. The backlight works well with your title in this case.It looks like the lights on each side of the entrance are on?  In archetectual shots like this, in order to get the lights to look good at dusk or after dark, a long exposure is used, and someone flips the lights on and off for just a blink. They show up good, and don''t blow out completely that way.', '2007-06-25 01:01:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3830665, 523556, 48228, '<td valign="top">I really do appriciate what you were saying here with this shot and it is so beautifull done..... I like it a lot.....</td>', 'I really do appriciate what you were saying here with this shot and it is so beautifull done..... I like it a lot.....', '2007-06-25 05:36:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842593, 524043, 60862, '<td valign="top">Very nice job with conveying a difficult, abstract concept.</td>', 'Very nice job with conveying a difficult, abstract concept.', '2007-06-27 17:15:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(3843745, 521511, 37818, '<td valign="top">I shoot in my church all the imte, but I can never acheive this kind of brightness and clarity of colour...lovely</td>', 'I shoot in my church all the imte, but I can never acheive this kind of brightness and clarity of colour...lovely', '2007-06-27 22:56:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3844124, 522839, 32997, '<td valign="top">this is quite intimidating...and that says a lot about religion, though I am not sure if that was your intent..<br/>th figure appears almost ghostlike...I really like the tones and it is verging on being too dark..I like that...</td>', 'this is quite intimidating...and that says a lot about religion, though I am not sure if that was your intent..th figure appears almost ghostlike...I really like the tones and it is verging on being too dark..I like that...', '2007-06-28 01:02:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3844307, 522839, 34113, '<td valign="top">The receding, parallel lines of the pews and desaturation really set off the lone worshiper in this strong image.</td>', 'The receding, parallel lines of the pews and desaturation really set off the lone worshiper in this strong image.', '2007-06-28 02:04:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3844315, 522839, 41047, '<td valign="top">the dark tones and grain work so well to set the mood. very emotive and strong image. well-done.</td>', 'the dark tones and grain work so well to set the mood. very emotive and strong image. well-done.', '2007-06-28 02:06:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3845452, 522975, 72579, '<td valign="top">THATS ME!!!!!</td>', 'THATS ME!!!!!', '2007-06-28 14:24:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3845779, 522839, 61651, '<td valign="top">Nice somberness to this - I think the noise/grain contributes to that effect, as if it muffles the image, but still allows us to see, much like the veil over the subject''s head.</td>', 'Nice somberness to this - I think the noise/grain contributes to that effect, as if it muffles the image, but still allows us to see, much like the veil over the subject''s head.', '2007-06-28 16:46:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3850200, 519818, 44877, '<td valign="top">This is just brilliant. So creative, interesting, gritty, arty, moving. Take pride in the mediocre score. Great art never appeals to the masses. :o)</td>', 'This is just brilliant. So creative, interesting, gritty, arty, moving. Take pride in the mediocre score. Great art never appeals to the masses. :o)', '2007-06-30 00:15:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3858324, 523175, 62925, '<td valign="top">I didn''t bother to read all these comments but who ever saying thats its a Mockery of Religion should think of what your saying. What is he mocking? <br/>Religion is something very personal and different people believe in different things, this photo isn''t bashing Christianity, Muslims, Atheists etc.<br/>Its just saying the model in this is praying to the toilet. I think sometimes people will twist a photos intent into making it something very personally and attack on the photographer.</td>', 'I didn''t bother to read all these comments but who ever saying thats its a Mockery of Religion should think of what your saying. What is he mocking? Religion is something very personal and different people believe in different things, this photo isn''t bashing Christianity, Muslims, Atheists etc.Its just saying the model in this is praying to the toilet. I think sometimes people will twist a photos intent into making it something very personally and attack on the photographer.', '2007-07-02 14:55:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3867854, 519422, 49865, '<td valign="top">Um, wow. This is incredible, the robed figure adds just the right, powerful touch needed in an already incredible landscape photo.</td>', 'Um, wow. This is incredible, the robed figure adds just the right, powerful touch needed in an already incredible landscape photo.', '2007-07-04 14:33:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3867866, 522563, 49865, '<td valign="top">This image captures the striking power of religion in the historical and contemporary world.</td>', 'This image captures the striking power of religion in the historical and contemporary world.', '2007-07-04 14:36:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3867884, 523915, 49865, '<td valign="top">I have to admit, a number of the contrasts in this image were lost on me until I read along with your description, but having done so this image went from "nice" to "great" in my mind. Most striking to me is the rigidity of the spike driver''s hands as compared to the open submission of the victim.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-07-04 13:41:38.</i></td>', 'I have to admit, a number of the contrasts in this image were lost on me until I read along with your description, but having done so this image went from "nice" to "great" in my mind. Most striking to me is the rigidity of the spike driver''s hands as compared to the open submission of the victim.', '2007-07-04 14:40:50.000000', '2007-07-04 14:41:38.000000', 0),
(3867895, 521274, 49865, '<td valign="top">Ahhh, Miyajima...</td>', 'Ahhh, Miyajima...', '2007-07-04 14:42:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3867907, 523455, 49865, '<td valign="top">This image may not be as evocative as the more symbolic or grandiose ones that placed higher, but the technical skill needed to pull this off is understandably quite impressive. The result is quite well done, and I''m glad you stuck with it until you got it to work. Nice job.</td>', 'This image may not be as evocative as the more symbolic or grandiose ones that placed higher, but the technical skill needed to pull this off is understandably quite impressive. The result is quite well done, and I''m glad you stuck with it until you got it to work. Nice job.', '2007-07-04 14:46:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3901336, 524008, 18780, '<td valign="top">How could 69 people give you average or worse scores on this fantastically toned shot? Well, it''s DP voting...I guess the number is significant.</td>', 'How could 69 people give you average or worse scores on this fantastically toned shot? Well, it''s DP voting...I guess the number is significant.', '2007-07-13 18:21:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3923161, 523175, 61552, '<td valign="top">"Praying to the Porceline God" is a cliche that means "throwing up in the toilet" and that''s all.  (That''s not a mockery of religion).<br/> <br/>Let he who has never prayed to the Porceline God cast the first stone!  (That IS a mockery of Christianity).<br/></td>', '"Praying to the Porceline God" is a cliche that means "throwing up in the toilet" and that''s all.  (That''s not a mockery of religion). Let he who has never prayed to the Porceline God cast the first stone!  (That IS a mockery of Christianity).', '2007-07-20 23:39:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4026133, 519818, 78196, '<td valign="top">An incredible image. There''s something quite ghostly and outwordly about it. It fascinates me and unsettles me at the same time. In short, a real work of art, and I mean that quite sincerely.</td>', 'An incredible image. There''s something quite ghostly and outwordly about it. It fascinates me and unsettles me at the same time. In short, a real work of art, and I mean that quite sincerely.', '2007-08-24 13:26:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4029160, 521124, 64795, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot.  Thanks for the comment! :)</td>', 'Very nice shot.  Thanks for the comment! :)', '2007-08-26 00:21:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4033161, 523326, 55883, '<td valign="top">Fantastic idea and photo, i really Love the two heart shadows.<br/>Thanks for creating such a beautiful photo :)</td>', 'Fantastic idea and photo, i really Love the two heart shadows.Thanks for creating such a beautiful photo :)', '2007-08-27 17:46:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4079869, 524084, 70484, '<td valign="top">I never did comment on this one. I really liked how it ended up. Very nice!</td>', 'I never did comment on this one. I really liked how it ended up. Very nice!', '2007-09-11 01:01:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4095377, 522884, 64994, '<td valign="top">Wow!! too cool!!<br/></td>', 'Wow!! too cool!!', '2007-09-17 02:15:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4121278, 524109, 28710, '<td valign="top">fantastic shot. No idea how you did that nail so convincingly. It really looks like it has pierced the foot.</td>', 'fantastic shot. No idea how you did that nail so convincingly. It really looks like it has pierced the foot.', '2007-09-27 22:43:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4123962, 524162, 30791, '<td valign="top">i love this!!!!</td>', 'i love this!!!!', '2007-09-29 06:15:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4169743, 524017, 53316, '<td valign="top">Really awesome image.</td>', 'Really awesome image.', '2007-10-15 17:27:07.000000', NULL, 0),
